1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:03,333
You wake up to a hen pecking at your hand.

2
00:00:03,430 --> 00:00:07,198
In your fist is all the money you have: one silver penny.

3
00:00:07,581 --> 00:00:10,363
And you need bread. Today.

4
00:00:11,313 --> 00:00:14,356
One room. Hens included.

5
00:00:14,405 --> 00:00:18,172
No chimney: smoke from the hearth drifts out through the thatch.

6
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:21,767
Bread means the market. Time to go.

7
00:00:23,317 --> 00:00:26,507
Welcome to England, around 1260.

8
00:00:26,602 --> 00:00:30,629
Four in five people live like you: in villages, farming.

9
00:00:30,763 --> 00:00:34,502
Timber frames, wattle-and-clay walls, roofs of thatch.

10
00:00:35,652 --> 00:00:38,851
HUGH THE BAKER: Fresh bread! A farthing a loaf!

11
00:00:38,962 --> 00:00:42,175
It's market day, and bread is serious business.

12
00:00:42,241 --> 00:00:45,967
By law, a loaf's weight was tied to the price of grain.

13
00:00:46,161 --> 00:00:51,249
Short-weight bakers were fined. Repeat offenders: the pillory.

14
00:00:52,099 --> 00:00:54,229
So you hold out your penny.

15
00:00:54,906 --> 00:00:59,934
HUGH THE BAKER: A whole penny? For one loaf? I've no change for that!

16
00:01:00,064 --> 00:01:04,468
The problem: the silver penny is the only coin in everyday use.

17
00:01:04,765 --> 00:01:09,623
That's about a day's pay. Your loaf costs a quarter of it.

18
00:01:10,673 --> 00:01:13,232
So the baker does something wild.

19
00:01:14,098 --> 00:01:18,380
He cuts your money in half. Then in half again.

20
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:22,058
Cut halfpennies and farthings were everyday change.

21
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:26,284
The cross runs to the coin's edge, and pieces were cut along it.

22
00:01:26,513 --> 00:01:29,627
That's what 'farthing' means: a fourth part.

23
00:01:30,677 --> 00:01:35,611
One quarter buys the loaf. Three go back in your purse.

24
00:01:35,997 --> 00:01:38,181
Not bad for your first day.

25
00:01:38,378 --> 00:01:42,437
But tomorrow at dawn, the lord's reeve expects you in his fields.

26
00:01:42,775 --> 00:01:45,934
Unpaid. That's your rent.
